{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>והארכת ימים</b> — by gematria: a world that is entirely long." "<b>והארכת ימים</b> — and adjacent to it: כי תבנה בית חדש. To say: if you built a new house, make it a parapet, so that days will be lengthened in it and they will not fall from it. Furthermore, the essence of length of days is for the building of a new house, which is the House of the Sanctuary. Therefore, even in honoring father and mother He preceded והארכת ימים to למען ייטב לך — not so here, in order to juxtapose והארכת ימים to כי תבנה בית חדש. Above it is written למען ייטב לך, and He juxtaposed here כי יפל הנופל ממנו — a hint to what they expounded: if one climbed a tree to send away the mother and fell and died, where is the length of days of this one?"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:10:17.977970140Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}